# ── OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db

# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key

# ── Go ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anchored to the repo root so it never matches the cmd/opencircuit/ source
# directory. An unanchored binary name matches at any depth and silently
# excludes source — this bit the ShortLinks repo (its issue #0001).
/opencircuit
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# ── Node / Vite ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.vite/

# The built SPA is generated by `npm run build` and embedded via //go:embed.
# dist/index.html is committed as a minimal placeholder so `go build ./...`
# compiles from a clean checkout before any npm build has run — do NOT commit
# a real built index.html over it.
web/dist/*
!web/dist/index.html

# ── Editors ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
*.swp

# ── Transient agent state ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
CERBERUS.md

# Subagent git worktrees. Anchored (leading slash) so it matches only the
# repo-root directory the agent runner creates — an unanchored pattern would
# match a `.claude/worktrees` at any depth. See CLAUDE.md §8: the same anchoring
# mistake on the binary name silently excluded cmd/opencircuit/ in ShortLinks.
/.claude/worktrees/

# ── Workshop cover images ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Workshop cover images are NOT part of this repository at all, and do not
# belong under web/public/ in any form -- tracked or ignored. They live on the
# server's own disk at /var/www/media, served directly by Apache's /media/
# carve-out, entirely outside web/public/ and the Go binary's embedded dist/.
# See docs/media.md for the full design and how to add one.
#
# This corrects a wrong premise (#0432): the *.jpg/*.jpeg rules that used to
# sit here (added 2026-09-04, issues/0416.md) assumed cover images belonged in
# web/public/ and merely shouldn't be tracked. They don't belong there at all.
# web/public/ holds only its 23 tracked, load-bearing design assets -- fonts,
# favicons, the logo and mark variants, the hero-crt webp set, og-default.png.
